@page "/Apps/SmsTicket/PrivacyPolicy"
@model MZikmund.Web.Pages.Apps.SmsTicketPrivacyPolicyModel
@{
    MetaTags.Title = "SMS Ticket Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="prose-page prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy for SMS Ticket</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 21 November 2026</p>

    <p>This privacy policy applies to the SMS Ticket app (SMS Jízdenka, hereby referred to as "Application") for mobile
        devices that was created by Martin Zikmund (hereby referred to as "Service Provider") as an Open Source service. The
        source code is available at <a href="https://github.com/MartinZikmund/SmsTicket">github.com/MartinZikmund/SmsTicket</a>.
        The Application prepares SMS messages for buying Czech public transport tickets.</p>

    <h2>Accounts and servers</h2>
    <p>The Application has no user accounts and no server of its own. The Service Provider does not collect, store or sell
        your personal data.</p>

    <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>The following data is stored only on your device and is removed when you uninstall the Application:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>settings (city, theme and language),</li>
        <li>favorite tickets,</li>
        <li>purchase history (which ticket was prepared and when),</li>
        <li>the text of ticket confirmation SMS messages, but only those you explicitly paste or share into the Application,
            or approve in Android's system SMS consent prompt.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>SMS messages</h2>
    <p>The Application never sends SMS messages itself. It opens your messaging app with a prepared message, and you send it
        yourself. The Application does not read your SMS inbox and does not have the SMS read permission.</p>
    <p>On Android, the Application uses Google's SMS User Consent API. It shows a single incoming message to the
        Application only after you approve it in a system dialog.</p>

    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>Location is used only if you tap "Use my location" or turn on "Select the nearest city on launch". The Application
        uses approximate location only, on your device, to pick the nearest city. Location is never stored or sent
        anywhere.</p>

    <h2>Notifications</h2>
    <p>The Application can show reminders before a ticket expires. These are local notifications scheduled on your device.
        No push notification service is used.</p>

    <h2>Ticket price data</h2>
    <p>Ticket price data is downloaded from GitHub (raw.githubusercontent.com). GitHub may log technical data such as your
        IP address, as described in the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General
            Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The Application shows banner ads from Google AdMob. Google may collect and use device identifiers (such as the
        advertising ID or IDFA), your IP address and usage data to serve and measure ads, and, with your consent, to
        personalize them.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, Google's consent form asks for your consent
            first. You can change your choice at any time in the Application under Settings, "Ad privacy settings".</li>
        <li>On iOS, Apple's App Tracking Transparency prompt controls tracking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps
            that use our services</a>.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The Application is not directed at children under the age of 13, and the Service Provider does not knowingly collect
        personal information from children.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Changes will be published on this page, and the "Last updated"
        date above will change.</p>

    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions regarding privacy while using the Application, please contact the Service Provider via
        email at <a href="mailto:martin@zikmund.dev">martin@zikmund.dev</a>.</p>
</div>
